.TH MIOS 7 "" "MiOS 0.3.0" "MiOS Concepts"
.SH NAME
mios \- what MiOS is and how its pieces relate
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
> Part I: Foundations & Philosophy of the [MiOS manual](../manual.md).
.PP
This chapter covers the documentation for **Introduction and Core Concepts** under MiOS.
.PP
> Path Reference: `/usr/share/doc/mios/manual.md#01_what_is_mios`
.PP
MiOS (pronounced *"MyOS"*) is a specialized operating system built to serve two roles simultaneously:
.PP
1. **Immutable Workstation**: It is a Fedora\-based, bootc\-native OCI container image. The entire OS is compiled, linted, and distributed as a single OCI container. The running system operates on a read\-only rootfs (`/usr` composefs/ostree mount), meaning updates are transactional (similar to a `git pull`) and rollbacks are atomic. 2. **Local Agentic AI OS**: It is a sovereign, self\-contained AI\-powered operating system. The desktop interface is tightly integrated with a local inference engine, model\-swapping proxies, an agent router, and pgvector semantic database memory. All agent tools, terminal interfaces, and desktop widgets interact with a unified local endpoint, enabling the system to inspect, run code, and configure itself completely offline.
.PP
